From ef628d10387074d2e32842b7b3c823927d0109ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:49:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 28/32] software_isp: Correct lens shading with a radial model

Phone camera modules darken towards the corners, and tint them, by a
stop or more; the software ISP shows that as it comes.

Add a radial lens shading correction: the GPU debayer multiplies each
colour by 1 + k1 r^2 + k2 r^4 after the black level, where r is the
distance from the centre of the sensor's active area over half its
diagonal, so one set of coefficients serves every mode. A new
LensShading algorithm in the simple IPA takes the coefficients for
red, green and blue from the tuning file, scales the radius for the
configured mode's crop, and supports LensShadingCorrectionEnable.

The CPU debayer doesn't apply it yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
